James inquired about how to properly mention a non-peer-reviewed chapter in a book on his academic resume. He suggested placing it in his "Peer-Reviewed Publications" section or the existing "Reports and Online Books" section. I advised him to keep non-peer-reviewed works separate from peer-reviewed articles and proposed renaming his section to "Chapters, Reports, and Online Books" or "Other Publications" for clarity. This title change would accommodate various publication types and enhance the organization of his resume. I also provided a structured format for listing the chapter to ensure proper attribution and delineation from peer-reviewed content.
